  "answer": "This feature has been requested before, but it isn't implemented yet. terminal#3637 asks for separate defaults when the Terminal is elevated, for example a `defaultsWhenElevated` section next to `profiles.defaults`. terminal#14593 asks for a different appearance when running as Administrator, and the team closed it as a duplicate of #8311, the issue for admin-specific schemes and themes. The team is tracking all admin-specific customizations in the epic terminal#11111. I didn't find #8311 itself in the archive. Please add your use case and the idea of different defaults for elevated windows to those issues. In the meantime, you can set `colorScheme` or `tabColor` on each profile you run elevated, but you can't set it for the whole elevated window."
